export abstract anchor FactoryConformance:
    conformanceScenarios:
        Conformance is required and is demonstrated through a typed checklist.
        Core scenarios are:
        - a fresh scaffold with a valid descriptor, six runnable commands, successful onboarding, and a loading dashboard
        - an order lifecycle with independent assessment and completion evidence
        - question blocking, answers, changed-answer revalidation, and successors
        - restart recovery, launch-gap adoption where token or lookup discovery supports it, duplicate-session containment, and no duplicate work; reference-only adapters must block and escalate without launching
        - confirmed, failed, and unconfirmed cancellation with preservation
        - budget reservation, delayed usage, priority admission, and overrun stop
        - plan conflict pause, merge, revalidation, and resume
        - per-writing-step isolation, pinned prerequisites, and cleanup after preservation
        - job capacity, priority, caching, retries, cancellation, recovery, and local-remote parity
        - wiring validation, repair, rollback, outage classification, and idempotency
        - duplicate requests, version conflicts, late outcomes, and late results
        - evidence manifests, redaction, retention, tombstones, and secrets
        Additional required scenarios cover status observability and
        cannot-start reasons, graceful shutdown, onboarding states and decision
        categories, credential references, configuration change restoration,
        adoption, stall detection and cause-routed escalation, deferred and
        partial delivery, the delivery matrix, the recovery matrix, the
        observability matrix, the authorization matrix, the lease matrix,
        adoption mapping and conformance, and unmerged-prerequisite
        reconciliation.
    harnessRecoveryMatrix:
        Harness recovery is tested in typed cells: harness, account kind,
        discovery mode, and fault. Faults are launch-gap, duplicate launch,
        client disconnect, confirmed death without result, harness restart,
        crash before launch, and a token belonging to another attempt. Each cell
        reports its own verdict, and external-effect counts are asserted with a
        quiescence window.
        Expected outcomes are: launch-gap adopts one session or establishes
        authoritative not-launched and then launches exactly once; duplicate
        launch yields one active session and one effect; disconnect reconnects
        without a launch; confirmed death retries only retry-safe effects;
        restart adopts surviving sessions with no launch; crash before launch
        launches exactly once; a wrong token is never adopted. Reference-only
        blocks the launch-gap cell without launching. Unsupported and
        not-applicable are not passing verdicts for a claimed supported
        harness; a launch-only mode needs an explicit engineer-approved
        exception.
    budgetConformance:
        Budget conformance uses typed cells: per-attempt usage, cumulative-only
        usage, delayed reading, out-of-order reading, duplicate reading, restart
        between reading and reconcile, mid-flight reset, provider-enforced
        ceiling, budget-unknown mode, unresolved exposure crossing, throttling,
        exhaustion, and paid fallback. Each cell records an expected
        observation.
        A positive control constructs an estimate greater than remaining
        capacity and asserts the refused dispatch with its budget reason while
        unrelated work on another account continues. Reconciliation completes
        only after readings are drained and the high-water mark is quiescent. A
        best-effort cell asserts dispatch stopped and the ledger reconciled. A
        provider-enforced cell asserts actual usage stayed within the ceiling. A
        budget-unknown cell asserts the accepted exposure bound and does not
        claim a hard cap.
